{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf","id":894191,"title":"Strix Possessed Werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-19T11:26:43-07:00","id":894191,"title":"Strix Possessed Werewolf?","content":"Because I am &quot;joyfully&quot; forced to use my phone until my internet is back up and running, I decided to pass the time with a fun little &quot;what if&quot; scenario. Now the fact that the Strix can apparently possess any major splat is bad enough ( even those who are thought to be impossible to possess), they are essentially no more powerful than ordinary mortal/dead/vampire hosts. Werewolves though... this is not the case. in fact aside from a vampire, a werewolf seems to be like a horribly, horribly ideal host for a young Strix seeking to wreak untold amounts of havoc or an older, more cunning Owl to possess a self sustaining vitae factory.. as well as indulging in the occasional week of mayhem, or three. As shapeshifting is apparently accessible for the Strix in a Uratha's body, I also had a horrifying notion occur to me: Since the Strix are essentially supernatural killing instinct and rage given a supervillain veneer of civility.. would Kuruth not be an issue either? And if so.. dear Luna what horrors could a nigh indestructible killing machine meat-suit ( save for the Strix banes) accomplish..?<br /> <br /> As always, what are your thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:05:40-07:00","id":894222,"title":"","content":"Oh dear god so much yes. I hope this is actually a thing that can be done. I'm entering a small game soon that mixes vampire, werewolf, and mage. Its more werewolf than anything else with a mage living in the pack, but the setting is the vampire's Montreal setting with the Nameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:05:48-07:00","id":894223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf#post894191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I am &quot;joyfully&quot; forced to use my phone until my internet is back up and running, I decided to pass the time with a fun little &quot;what if&quot; scenario. Now the fact that the Strix can apparently possess any major splat is bad enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding Strix could only possess <i>corpses</i>, both mundane and (through a quirk of their template they qualify as corpses while animate) vampires. I may be wrong on that though, and if I am please cite the reference so I can correct mistaken belief. If I am correct that means Strix could possess the corpses of any major splat, but it could be argued (correctly or not) a dead mage or werewolf no longer house their soul which is the seat of their supernatural power, as opposed to vampires.<br /> <br /> Walking around with the body of a dead werewolf, even if it no longer has the werewolf template, can cause insane trouble both in the werewolf and vampire communities, and is itself a terrifying prospect for players in either splat.<br /> <br /> I am hopeful this adds something meaning to the conversation, and am interested to hear back from the Original Poster and the community.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 05-19-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:24:07-07:00","id":894232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894223#post894223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my understanding Strix could only possess <i>corpses</i>, both mundane and (through a quirk of their template they qualify as corpses while animate) vampires. I may be wrong on that though, and if I am please cite the reference so I can correct mistaken belief. If I am correct that means Strix could possess the corpses of any major splat, but it could be argued (correctly or not) a dead mage or werewolf no longer house their soul which is the seat of their supernatural power, as opposed to vampires.<br /> <br /> Walking around with the body of a dead werewolf, even if it no longer has the werewolf template, can cause insane trouble both in the werewolf and vampire communities, and is itself a terrifying prospect for players in either splat.<br /> <br /> I am hopeful this adds something meaning to the conversation, and am interested to hear back from the Original Poster and the community.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In second ed, Strix have access to Embodiments, which represent what they can possess/ how they can express themselves in the world around them through their shadow-y nature. There is an Embodiment called Possess Living, which allows the strix to well, possess living beings. What makes this differ from first ed is that the body can survive the possession, and as long as the Strix continues to maintain it through eating/ drinking ( which is unlikely, though strix who are smart/ enjoy living bodies typically try to do so at least for a little while.). Werewolves are interesting because while the Strix can't use the Uratha's spirit magic any more than it can use a mages' spells or a Mummie's Utterances or Affinities, they can make use of the body's natural abilities such as regeneration.. or shape shifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:26:49-07:00","id":894234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894222#post894222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear god so much yes. I hope this is actually a thing that can be done. I'm entering a small game soon that mixes vampire, werewolf, and mage. Its more werewolf than anything else with a mage living in the pack, but the setting is the vampire's Montreal setting with the Nameless.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be, though the particulars are as always up to the ST. still, I remember the Blood &amp; Smoke book stating that regeneration and shape shifting still operate more or less as normal, which lead to this terrifying epiphany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:58:06-07:00","id":894253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf#post894191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I am &quot;joyfully&quot; forced to use my phone until my internet is back up and running, I decided to pass the time with a fun little &quot;what if&quot; scenario. Now the fact that the Strix can apparently possess any major splat is bad enough ( even those who are thought to be impossible to possess), they are essentially no more powerful than ordinary mortal/dead/vampire hosts. Werewolves though... this is not the case. in fact aside from a vampire, a werewolf seems to be like a horribly, horribly ideal host for a young Strix seeking to wreak untold amounts of havoc or an older, more cunning Owl to possess a self sustaining vitae factory.. as well as indulging in the occasional week of mayhem, or three. As shapeshifting is apparently accessible for the Strix in a Uratha's body, I also had a horrifying notion occur to me: Since the Strix are essentially supernatural killing instinct and rage given a supervillain veneer of civility.. would Kuruth not be an issue either? And if so.. dear Luna what horrors could a nigh indestructible killing machine meat-suit ( save for the Strix banes) accomplish..?<br /> <br /> As always, what are your thoughts on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When reading the Embodiments section I had the exact same idea. I was already going to throw some kind of werewolf abomination thing at my crossover group and this made be go &quot;yup, that's the one!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:09:54-07:00","id":894266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894253#post894253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When reading the Embodiments section I had the exact same idea. I was already going to throw some kind of werewolf abomination thing at my crossover group and this made be go &quot;yup, that's the one!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had that thought too, though this is infinitely cooler than owod Abominations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:20:42-07:00","id":894276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894266#post894266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had that thought too, though this is infinitely cooler than owod Abominations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, I didnt mean that specific kind of abomination, I was just using the word in general use. I was thinking more of a werewolf revenent/ghost/spirit-magath thing, basically showing that there is something WRONG here. I think a strix counts for that in my case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:00:45-07:00","id":894302,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah it can certainly be done. You would have a dark wolf of sorts. My only problem with it is that, to me, the best part of the strix is their ability to possess and move to different bodies, and you lose something with that with a permanent host. But they do have a lot of neat abilities that could be used aside from the possession, necromantic-feeling powers, and a werewolf has hefty abilities on its own. Their senses and shapeshifting alone are enough to help a strix wreak havoc on a vampire population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:30:14-07:00","id":894323,"title":"","content":"This is answered by the &quot;Stranger Hosts&quot; sidebar on page 206.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why should vampires have all the fun? The Strix can attempt to possess other supernatural creatures just as easily as revenants and the Kindred. Possessing Sin-Eaters, Mummies, and Prometheans requires \u201cPossess Kindred,\u201d while possessing Werewolves, Mages, Changelings, and Demons requires \u201cPossess Living.\u201d Strix inside supernatural hosts cannot access any powers held in the soul \u2014 they can\u2019t use a mage-host\u2019s powers, a mummy host immediately dies and becomes a corpse-host, a werewolf-host can\u2019t use Gifts \u2014 but purely physical powers such as a werewolf\u2019s shapechanging may still be accessible at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Advantages like Mana, Glamour, and Essence don\u2019t convert to Vitae, but living hosts can still be farmed as described under Possess Living. Where things get really strange is if the Strix then attempts to use Synthesis on a supernatural host. Unique monsters and aberrant powers result. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:34:26-07:00","id":894325,"title":"","content":"Doesn't &quot;victims&quot; of Strix possession need to have been somehow tainted with vitae somehow first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:41:29-07:00","id":894331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894325#post894325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't &quot;victims&quot; of Strix possession need to have been somehow tainted with vitae somehow first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noooooooope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:04:38-07:00","id":894346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894325#post894325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't &amp;quot;victims&amp;quot; of Strix possession need to have been somehow tainted with vitae somehow first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no my friend, they can be perfectly clean~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:20:57-07:00","id":894355,"title":"","content":"Now for the important question: Do you think a Strix could use its host to do a permanent, full powered Garu form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:23:31-07:00","id":894358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894355#post894355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for the important question: Do you think a Strix could use its host to do a permanent, full powered Garu form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. They'd not be able to use the Gifts for it unless you decided they had an interesting Synthesis. I think you could allow for the Shadow Gifts if the strix possessed a spirit first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:12:07-07:00","id":894645,"title":"","content":"You get &quot;tainted with vitae&quot; the moment the strix forces itself down your throat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:03:38-07:00","id":894787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894358#post894358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why not. They'd not be able to use the Gifts for it unless you decided they had an interesting Synthesis. I think you could allow for the Shadow Gifts if the strix possessed a spirit first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why not. they don't have the rage that drives them they don't have the primal power of a werewolf. It doesn't make sense for them to have full garou abilities. I'd treat it like the gift where you can take werewolf form but don't suffer from the rage. They are a bit underpowered but it's still a powerful creature able to rend kindred apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T23:44:40-07:00","id":895344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894787#post894787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see why not. they don't have the rage that drives them they don't have the primal power of a werewolf. It doesn't make sense for them to have full garou abilities. I'd treat it like the gift where you can take werewolf form but don't suffer from the rage. They are a bit underpowered but it's still a powerful creature able to rend kindred apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the Strix are rage, they are primal killing instinct given immaterial form. That sounds pretty fitting to make use of Garu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T03:43:57-07:00","id":895408,"title":"","content":"See, that's the weird thing. If they <i>are</i> the Beast, as they often claim, then they're totally all about rage and murder when they're stuck in a vampire. Outside of one, though, they're generally pretty chill. I mean, they'll still murder you for fun, but they won't be particularly angry about anything when they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T04:36:29-07:00","id":895415,"title":"","content":"Strix are actually closer to the embodiment of ennui, rather than rage. Strix are the embodiment of the &quot;bored vamprie elder&quot; syndrome that causes trouble just for that surge of fun and mischief, so they can feel some emotion. Sure, they were pissed at the Julii, but that was concluded. Sure, the Owls of Dis hate vampires, but that's more of a case of jealousy, not anger or rage. Vampires, for all their banes, have it better than the strix, and they want what vampires get. The Owls see the humanity of vampires as a perversion of their nature. &quot;The Owls\u2019 hatred is cold, not the abandon of Kindred frenzy.&quot; <br /> <br /> So, when it comes to Rage? I don't really see it as a thing. I mean, hells. Strix can't even <i>frenzy</i> as a vampire. They never lose control. Tying back to the elder-vampire syndrome, the strix are all about vengence-best-served-cold. Hot emotions like rage are pretty unlike the strix modus operandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T09:03:41-07:00","id":895513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=894787#post894787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why not. they don't have the rage that drives them they don't have the primal power of a werewolf. It doesn't make sense for them to have full garou abilities. I'd treat it like the gift where you can take werewolf form but don't suffer from the rage. They are a bit underpowered but it's still a powerful creature able to rend kindred apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want, you could have their gauru form act as the equivalent of the Father's Form Wolf Gift. But Empty Wolves, werewolves who have had their souls removed and replaced with spirits or souls, have no problem going into gauru form with all its benefits, so I don't see why a strix would have any problems with it.","signature":"","edite