ned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:17:52-07:00","id":897517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897511#post897511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you were saying just now that dispatching them was easy. Make up your mind, would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy yes. Safe, no. Its easy to pick up a bar of uranium with your bare hand, doesn't mean its safe to do so. Same concept lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T21:51:15-07:00","id":897569,"title":"","content":"Alright, you might be the only person that read the book and came to the conclusion that dealing with Strix is easy. Congrats, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T00:04:26-07:00","id":897617,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;deceptively simple&quot; would be a better term. How do you kill a strix? Easy. Just <i>totally immolate</i> its host. Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T04:39:29-07:00","id":897684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897617#post897617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;deceptively simple&quot; would be a better term. How do you kill a strix? Easy. Just <i>totally immolate</i> its host. Good luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that is a better way to put it, yeah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-24-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T04:41:28-07:00","id":897685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897569#post897569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, you might be the only person that read the book and came to the conclusion that dealing with Strix is easy. Congrats, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the only one, I know of several others.. merely the only one here lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:17:46-07:00","id":897730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897417#post897417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm surprised people don't think they have any rage.... They are described as having &quot;eternal anger&quot; and seem to hate basically everything.</div> </div> </div> </div> Jealous hatred is different from rage. Strix are the kinds of undead that hate the living for having life energy when the Owls do not; you see them all the time in stories. The Owls' hatred is cold, whereas rage is a hot emotion that triggers the fight-flight responce in living beings. In fact, the inability to have hot emotions is one of the primary reasons they steal bodies - so they can experience them. <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As for the whole easy-to-kill bit? That's true... in a white room. In game play, its actually far less so. Its like a gamer looking at D&amp;D's monster manual, then describing a way to kill off the Tarrasque or Tiamat or some other high level threat without actually taking into account the GM's strategies. Yes, in theory, its easy to kill a monster with XYZ situation. But the chance of that situation coming up is small, or any number of other factors come into play. This isn't that different than any other ephemeral being's bane - if you can arrange for its use in a proper way, you can stand a good chance of winning. But if you can't, its a hell of a fight.<br /> <br /> And immolating someone is not easy, even for non-vampire supernaturals with access to fire magic. Remember that most strix will be encountered possessing bodies, and if you set that body on fire, the strix isn't immobilized. Even when using Elemental Gifts or Contracts of the Elements, it is difficult to pin down one of the Owls that starts off in a corpse. Heaven forbid having a vampire body with Resilience, or some other supernatural with healing / damage reduction powers.<br /> <br /> In truth, the only &quot;easy&quot; way of killing a strix that I've found through game play involves using Shadow powers like the Khaibit or Death Arcana to manipulate the shadow forms the strix rely on. Maybe something with Influence (Shadows/Darkness) could help as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:22:15-07:00","id":897734,"title":"","content":"Before this derails further, lets keep in mind that a strix inhabiting a body through Possess Living or Synthesis is no longer a malevolent wisp of darkness and smoke. Further, while with Possess Living if a host dies the strix can still leave, with Synthesis the bond is permanent.<br /> <br /> The strix doesn't need to feel things if its host body does. And if it performs Synthesis it seems as if the body is going to affect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:07:54-07:00","id":897774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897730#post897730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Jealous hatred is different from rage. Strix are the kinds of undead that hate the living for having life energy when the Owls do not; you see them all the time in stories. The Owls' hatred is cold, whereas rage is a hot emotion that triggers the fight-flight responce in living beings. In fact, the inability to have hot emotions is one of the primary reasons they steal bodies - so they can experience them.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As for the whole easy-to-kill bit? That's true... in a white room. In game play, its actually far less so. Its like a gamer looking at D&amp;D's monster manual, then describing a way to kill off the Tarrasque or Tiamat or some other high level threat without actually taking into account the GM's strategies. Yes, in theory, its easy to kill a monster with XYZ situation. But the chance of that situation coming up is small, or any number of other factors come into play. This isn't that different than any other ephemeral being's bane - if you can arrange for its use in a proper way, you can stand a good chance of winning. But if you can't, its a hell of a fight.<br /> <br /> And immolating someone is not easy, even for non-vampire supernaturals with access to fire magic. Remember that most strix will be encountered possessing bodies, and if you set that body on fire, the strix isn't immobilized. Even when using Elemental Gifts or Contracts of the Elements, it is difficult to pin down one of the Owls that starts off in a corpse. Heaven forbid having a vampire body with Resilience, or some other supernatural with healing / damage reduction powers.<br /> <br /> In truth, the only &quot;easy&quot; way of killing a strix that I've found through game play involves using Shadow powers like the Khaibit or Death Arcana to manipulate the shadow forms the strix rely on. Maybe something with Influence (Shadows/Darkness) could help as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and what is this but a giant white room? XD. And I am perfectly aware of gameplay and story segregation, though I do greatly disagree on the difficulty of immolating a body/ human or otherwise with how tilts and conditions work based on personal experience in game,.. but neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Never thought to use the Khaibit actually, they are too specialized in second edition for me to use them unless I am going to do a spirit/ Strix heavy game.. which is ironic for a topic such as this, as the game by definition would be Strix/Spirit heavy... I simply see them as too few in number to be reasonably near by in this sort of situation.<br /> <br /> As for rage being strictly a hot emotion, that's not quite true in every case. For example, I am incredibly calm when I am legitimately, greatly angered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-24-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:12:32-07:00","id":897775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=897734#post897734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before this derails further, lets keep in mind that a strix inhabiting a body through Possess Living or Synthesis is no longer a malevolent wisp of darkness and smoke. Further, while with Possess Living if a host dies the strix can still leave, with Synthesis the bond is permanent.<br /> <br /> The strix doesn't need to feel things if its host body does. And if it performs Synthesis it seems as if the body is going to affect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Synthesis is a really vaguely written Embodiment to me... every time I read it I am just like &quot;are they actually fused? doesn't look like it..&quot;<br /> <br /> Synthesis with a werewolf Host would be interesting.. especially if the werewolf died and was then Embraced.. Chiropteran warform maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:02:01-07:00","id":897807,"title":"","content":"Synthesis makes a lot more sense if you look at the beast of the resulting vampire(-like thing) as the original strix and the leftovers as an offshoot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:10:43-07:00","id":897813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_contai