er","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:36:27-07:00","id":898227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=898162#post898162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and a fourth! Yesh, forums!</div> </div> </div> </div>how wonderful lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:53:04-07:00","id":898255,"title":"","content":"Umm... what happened to my actual post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:38:23-07:00","id":898436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=898255#post898255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... what happened to my actual post?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good question...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T10:25:29-07:00","id":902128,"title":"","content":"I think a Strix would need to synthesize a werewolf to use anything other than its basic shapeshifting, but if it simply possesses a werewolf then would only have access to basic shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> I would also chance a guess this would remove all of the werewolf's renown since this seems tied to their primal urge, but, who can say? Maybe the resultant creature could continue to dupe wolves and revel in that Rage it couldn't fully feel before.<br /> <br /> I personally don't like synthesis as written, mostly because I'm a Mage player and can't help but be a bit powergamey, and I like my other splats to be able to pick up the pace in the scary department so that my mage-centric worlds still have plenty to be afraid of--as such, I prefer to homerule my vampires to be a looot scarier than they are in the RAW. I so far can't tell/don't think werewolves need the same treatment, because always being in a pack and ganging up on something is a huge advantage.<br /> <br /> I wasn't quite sure if synthesis let the resulting creature keep the Strix's dread powers, but just think for a moment how scary it would be to be up against a Cahalith Storm Lord who is now a Strix that has the Labyrinth Dread Power and you were in a meat packing plant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:00:43-07:00","id":902142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902128#post902128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Strix would need to synthesize a werewolf to use anything other than its basic shapeshifting, but if it simply possesses a werewolf then would only have access to basic shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by basic shape-shifting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902128#post902128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also chance a guess this would remove all of the werewolf's renown since this seems tied to their primal urge, but, who can say? Maybe the resultant creature could continue to dupe wolves and revel in that Rage it couldn't fully feel before.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in the text that says renown is tied to primal urge, beyond a template consideration and that would be RAI at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902128#post902128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't like synthesis as written, mostly because I'm a Mage player and can't help but be a bit powergamey, and I like my other splats to be able to pick up the pace in the scary department so that my mage-centric worlds still have plenty to be afraid of--as such, I prefer to homerule my vampires to be a looot scarier than they are in the RAW. I so far can't tell/don't think werewolves need the same treatment, because always being in a pack and ganging up on something is a huge advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires aren't scary in the raw physicality that the average Uratha is. Vampires inconspicuously get involved into your life and then own you like you're their pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru