follow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then who is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed link between Uratha and humans, exemplar Hunter in Darkness depicted in Tribes of the Moon. Each time he took the Hishu form, however rare that he did, it was a from a new race. About as old as Red Sticks, if not older. Never fell into slumber and was a chosen champion of Black Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:34:25-07:00","id":902327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902306#post902306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Stick is so laughably not scary. Predator Kings typically aren't to me. If you're not Forsaken, he has nothing to do with you usually.. unless he wants some (literal) sugar. Strong and a tough werewolf certainly, but not that &quot;scary&quot;. And the wolf in the woods is that girl who has like two Unihar kids right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Mary, introduced as 'Babe in the Woods.' Wolf of the Woods is a very high Primal Urge werewolf who may have been born a wolf and may have sired an Uratha messiah with another wolf. Wolf and Red Sticks are probably the most powerful werewolves to have write-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:55:27-07:00","id":902334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902325#post902325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Missed link between Uratha and humans, exemplar Hunter in Darkness depicted in Tribes of the Moon. Each time he took the Hishu form, however rare that he did, it was a from a new race. About as old as Red Sticks, if not older. Never fell into slumber and was a chosen champion of Black Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I remenber. Yeah I have to say that girl who keeps fucking other werewolves is scarier. Just being strong and an exemplar werewolf isn't scary. Now if you're prey sure, but werewolves are only scary in certain situations compared to other monsters. Then again, werewolves don't scare me. Now spirit children who should not be, those are scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:17:38-07:00","id":902346,"title":"","content":"Though all these pale in comparison to the scariness of an immortal psychopathic bird joyriding in a body that makes vampire regeneration look expensive. (Though really it is, now that I think of it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:02:15-07:00","id":902781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894191-strix-possessed-werewolf?p=902142#post902142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by basic shape-shifting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just mean it is basic to their template. You could &quot;have a werewolf&quot; without gifts but you can't have a werewolf without its 5 forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> There's nothing in the text that says renown is tied to primal urge, beyond a template consideration and that would be RAI at most. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's true I guess. But doesn't renown come from the Lunes? Why would the Lunes give renown to anything else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires aren't scary in the raw physicality that the average Uratha is. Vampires inconspicuously get involved into your life and then own you like you're their pet. </div> </div> </div>I am more than aware of this, perfectly aware of this. It's just not enough for me, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T01:36:12-07:00","id":903333,"title":"","content":"Using the soulless wolves as an example, the spirits wouldn't give out renown to a non werewolf.<br /> <br /> They don't lose the renown they already have though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}